EXT. OPEN OCEAN - LIFEBOAT - DAY

A cracked orange lifeboat drifts on a flat grey sea. No land. PETRA ISAKSSON (30s, sunburned, hair matted) bails with a cut-off bottle. WILFRED OKONJO-HART (50s, one arm in a sling) watches the horizon. NOOR SAFFARINI (20s, lips split) lies across the thwart, eyes shut.

                    PETRA
          Water's rising.

                    WILFRED
          Keep bailing.

                    NOOR
          (without opening her eyes)
          Someone's out there.

                    WILFRED
          You're dreaming.

                    NOOR
          I'm not.

A splash. Petra freezes. Wilfred squints.

A man's head breaks the surface twenty feet off. A SWIMMER (30s, shaved head, black wetsuit, mouth ringed in salt) stroking toward them with long, tired, unhurried pulls.

                    PETRA
          Oh my God.

                    WILFRED
          Pull him in.

They grab his wrists. He thumps over the gunwale and lies there gasping. Petra offers the bottle. He drinks, coughs, drinks again.

                    SWIMMER
          Thank you.

                    WILFRED
          Where did you come from?

                    SWIMMER
          The cargo ship. It sank four days ago.

                    NOOR
          Four days?

                    SWIMMER
          Four days. I'm Ramon.

                    PETRA
          Ramon. Petra. This is Wilfred. That's Noor.

                    RAMON
          How many are you?

                    WILFRED
          Three.

                    RAMON
          Four, now.

He smiles. Noor opens one eye, and does not smile back.
